📗
  🎖 Tokens: it issues signed tokens (JSON Web Tokens, RFC 7519) and checks
  them. A token is three parts of base64url with dots between: a header, the
  claims, and a signature over the first two, made with HMAC-SHA-256 and a
  key that only the issuer and the checker have.

    🆕🎖 key❗️ ➡️ tokens
    ✍️ tokens 🔤ada🔤 claims now❗️ ➡️ token        💭 for ada, with these claims
    🔍 tokens token now❗️ ➡️ checked               💭 a 🎗: the claims, or why not

  One way of signing is taken, HS256, and a token that says it was signed
  another way, or not at all, is refused before its signature is looked at.
  The time is handed in, in seconds since 1970. Every setter returns the
  tokens.
