  📗
    Checks *text* as a token at *now*, and gives a 🎗: the claims of a token
    that holds, or the reason it is refused for. In this order: its shape
    (three parts of base64url, 8,192 characters at most); its header (HS256
    and nothing else, a type of JWT when it names one, nothing that "must
    be understood"); its signature, over the first two parts as they came;
    its claims (a JSON object); its end, which it has to have; that it is
    not from the future; and its issuer and audience, when the tokens were
    told whom to expect.
